     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><a href=\"https://gist.github.com/dmattek/7e4593a1acc0ace7c9f44073fc10670f.js\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://gist.github.com/dmattek/7e4593a1acc0ace7c9f44073fc10670f.js&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792389901251000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2pcrGQo-9BZg4ZHBmZErAR\">Here&#39;s</a> a simple app that allows to download data as a CSV file. The data is a simple random vector with length set by a slider.<div><br></div><div>Then I wrapped the download button in a module (<a href=\"https://gist.github.com/dmattek/ede3ef8ae097de228b703f5ae916e1d9.js\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://gist.github.com/dmattek/ede3ef8ae097de228b703f5ae916e1d9.js&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792389901252000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0nCGfZHtwypl3Dg3jFoIEI\">code here</a>). The server part contains a function with two arguments (name of the data file and the data vector itself) but it doesn&#39;t react to slider changes. I guess the issue is with passing the arguments which remain static upon function calls. How to fix that?</div><div><br></div><div>Many thanks for suggestions!</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
